{"body":{"asks":"The root reserves gestures and sets the rules of the game, as OpenLight's input floor did; otherwise input is the components'. A gesture, a left or right press or a combination, passes up the holarchy of drawings until captured, the same on any chassis. Is bubbling ever stopped; does a press on a button propagate, or is it deliberately caught; and is a component catching presses and keys itself an antipattern, save input changing only what it was given? The author: the root's reservations, of clicks and keys, must be data, a contract as the layers are.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC001"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Input reserved at the root, propagated until captured"}
{"body":{"asks":"Right-click is reserved at the root for the context menu, given the place pressed within the holarchy, and the menu component does the expression work from there: pure matching, no scope adding entries, nothing caught and no side effect. Perhaps each level up the tree is a label with its actions, global actions at the bottom, as seeing the layout as nodes. The agents found matching offering too much where most functions take any holon, and the place pressed unknown where a component in code draws a holon in its own markup. What would it hold? Pressing a function means nothing unless its output is handled; the address and navigation have no place in it; the only entries the author can think of now are choosing a component and opening the inspector; whether the address should have actions at all he doubts, while the history's back could.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC003"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"The context menu as matching over the holarchy"}
{"body":{"asks":"Whatever is mounted in a slot is agnostic and decoupled, and implements no chrome; chrome is apart from accessibility. The parent giving the card and background, a component being its content, seemed to the author smart and sane, though nesting troubles it, as a collation nests; perhaps some drawing at each slot's level. Each component library ships its own style, ours cards, another borders, the chassis caring for none: a wrapper component presenting its slot and drawing around it, perhaps reaching every slot beneath a reader as an offer, everything wrapped with some wrappers drawing nothing, or wrapping toggled. Wrapping as offers the author holds maybe reasonable but unexplored, whether the reader offers it or the wrapper takes it unknown, and what toggling does to the tree too; to be reasoned about further. A focus ring and a selection are chrome too, as OpenLight's reader gave collation selections their colours. Hosts today are display: contents and carry no box. The author does not know yet whether chrome can wait, it being connected with everything.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC004"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Chrome around nested components"}
{"body":{"asks":"A component in code that draws a holon in its own markup, as Value a card and prose a link, hides it from the chassis, which knows only that Value drew there; the inspector reads attributes the components set to find it. Layout as data has no such gap, and leaf components being code makes sense, though components as code have an obvious limitation. The author: any io.draw should contribute to the hierarchy, so, he guessed, it is the chassis's to keep, not code's to project; rows and the like should be components; a table its own kit, table, row and cell, since cells align, each clickable as a component of its own. Where code draws without io.draw is not yet worth reaching.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC008"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Holons drawn inside components in code"}
{"body":{"asks":"Completion is wanted in various kinds of input, driven over the buffer typed into and over the whole field it completes against. If it must be defined at the root and linked to the reader, the reader is not whole and two sources must be managed; would another reader need the same? There has to be a simple, pure and honourable way. The author wondered whether it is just written as an expression, shown if the buffer has contents; the session worked this out as completion as data in Search's layout, shown in the overlay layer while the buffer has text; the author does not yet trust the approach.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7002"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY7009","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Completion as a modality"}
{"body":{"asks":"Choosing which component draws a place modifies the holarchy itself, a WYSIWYG modification and not an action, and there are definitely more WYSIWYG actions; io.pick, given to components, was never asked for and is premature, and should not exist. Value's cards, rows and table modes, kept in the browser's storage, are the same choosing made by hand. Of a piece with the thread The interface open by nesting and choice.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7004"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M89280APGY700B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Choosing a component edits the holarchy"}
{"body":{"asks":"Perhaps the inspector is a layer of its own: what one hovers outlined, with some information around it, and an overlay telling more; it builds on wrapping, on layers and on what is there now, and may be too far yet, though the author finds it worth exploring further.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7005"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY700C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"The inspector as a layer"}
{"body":{"asks":"If typing in the expression bar is too laggy, the work cannot proceed so: it must be resolved, though after the first things. Typing only updates the buffer, which only completion and the input care about, so he does not expect the whole page to render again. One read for a turn was meant to be dissected so components do not render again, yet makes the engine's read longer, and latency matters for what is as real-time as typing; and separate reads and subscriptions would make each smaller; but each kept read stands on every store, so a buffer moving on a keystroke runs all again. With commits tracking where a holon exists, everything brought into another store shipped with where it came from, a read could stand only on the stores that can hold what it read: the threads Where a holon is kept and Holding links to history. Not what was tried before (21/87, 21/93). The reverse calculation in the engine sounds complicated and is postponed, and the engine need not change yet (23/48); the take on the store and the history of commits is something to explore.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M89280APGY7006"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M89280APGY700D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Typing kept fast"}